**Medium Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
`LocalDev` and `AbsoluteGitHookPath` in settings are only ever set to `true`, never cleared to `false`. In `runEnableInteractive`, the old code `settings.LocalDev = localDev` unconditionally synced the setting with the flag value. The new code `if opts.LocalDev { settings.LocalDev = true }` only sets it, meaning re-running `entire enable` without `--local-dev` or `--absolute-git-hook-path` leaves stale `true` values in settings. Hooks are installed using `opts` (correct), but later calls to `EnsureSetup()` or `setupGitHook()` read the stale setting and could reinstall hooks with the unwanted configuration.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

